Vite `fs.allow` is the app dir only (not the vault); the dev-server guard
(`isForbiddenDevFsRequest` in server/request-guard.ts, wired in vite.config.ts) returns 403 for any
`/@fs/` request outside the app dir or under the vault, in encoded/backslash/case variants.
`/api/graph/refresh` additionally requires an allowed-or-absent Origin, `Sec-Fetch-Site`
same-origin/none (if present) and header `X-Jarvis-Refresh: 1` (sent by the Settings button).

Vite's HMR WebSocket additionally gets an Origin allow-list (upgrade listener in
vite.config.ts); Vite 5.4.21 itself enforces Host (allowedHosts) and the ws token.
server/graph-worker.ts loads content-path.ts by explicit file URL (tsx does not remap
relative specifiers inside worker threads) and vite.config.ts excludes tests/** from vitest.

The dev-request guard also rejects, for all URLs, any '.'/'..' segment after repeated
percent-decoding and backslash folding, any URL mentioning the vault directory name, and
dotfile segments (except node_modules/.vite).

