Remaining limitations
  - Browser rendering, CSP and browser-side external requests unverified.
  - File/directory symlink and file-swap race tests not run (no privilege); a junction case ran.
  - A WebSocket with no Origin header is accepted by design (Host and token still required).
  - The process is not sandboxed; the check-then-use race is narrowed, not eliminated; hardlinks undetected.
  - Incident: an unguarded `vitest run` during setup loaded the upstream branch of vite.config.ts and read the
    real ~/.jarvis-config.yaml (contents not printed or used). Rule: always run vite/vitest/tsx with the
    project-mode env.

  - Dev guard also denies non-source runtime artifacts anywhere in a dev URL (per path segment, case-insensitive,
    after repeated decoding): *.log *.err *.out *.tsbuildinfo *.pid *.bak *.orig *.swp *.tmp *.env *.pem *.key,
    optimization-log.json, MODIFICATIONS[.ext], .env*; plus NTFS ADS (name:stream, except after /@id/),
    trailing dot/space segments. server/request-guard.ts DEV_DENY_SEGMENT_PATTERNS.
  - Launcher logs go to <project>\.local\run\ (gitignored, outside appDir), not vendor\jarvis.
  - Kanban caps: title 160, evidence 600, deliverable/blocker/next action 300 (was 120/200); 64 KB record cap and
    25 tasks per column unchanged.

